   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T7"><text:span text:style-name="T7">You can provide an audio recording for the question and for each answer. The recording can be done in a program like Audacity (</text:span><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="https://www.audacityteam.org/" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T7">https://www.audacityteam.org</text:span></text:span></text:a><text:span text:style-name="T7">). Use </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T11">File</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T7"> &gt; </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T11">Export</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T7"> &gt; </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T11">Export Selected Audio</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T7">.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P32" loext:marker-style-name="T7"><text:span text:style-name="T7">In Reading App Builder, you need to put the audio clip (MP3 file) in the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T11">Audio Clips </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T7">tab for the quiz book.</text:span></text:p>
